# Shell scripts must keep LF endings in the working tree.
#
# `deploy/web-entrypoint.sh` and `server/docker-entrypoint.sh` are COPYed into
# Linux images and exec'd. A CRLF checkout gives the shebang a trailing \r, and
# the kernel then looks for an interpreter literally named "/bin/sh\r" — the
# container dies with "not found" and no useful diagnostic. Git stores these as
# LF, so CI on Linux is unaffected; without this file a Windows checkout builds
# a broken image locally.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning: read by a shell inside a container.
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
